{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019iM5CogHL2XHLKBhCqU695","type":"tool_result","content":"# Context: the Shelf service\n\nA gRPC server (Go, `google.golang.org/grpc`) over a SQLite file. The contract is `proto/toy/v1/shelf.proto`; the\nbehaviour is `REQUIREMENTS.md` / `spec.py`. You build the server; you do not change the proto, the spec, the harness,\nthe generator or this file.\n\n* **Stubs.** `gen/toy/v1/*.pb.go` is produced by `./generate.sh` (buf) from the proto and is rebuilt by every\n  `./check.sh`. Never write or edit anything under `gen/`. Import it as `toyv1 \"example.com/toybuild/gen/toy/v1\"`.\n* **Entry point.** A `package main` at the repository root (`go build -o bin/toy-server .`).\n* **Environment the checker sets.** `PORT`: listen for gRPC on `127.0.0.1:$PORT` (plaintext). `DB_PATH`: the SQLite file;\n  the table `items(id integer primary key autoincrement, name text not null unique, qty integer not null)` already\n  exists (the harness created it): do not create or migrate tables. Use `database/sql` with the pure-Go driver\n  `modernc.org/sqlite` (driver name `\"sqlite\"`; open `file:<DB_PATH>?_pragma=busy_timeout(10000)` and\n  `SetMaxOpenConns(1)`).\n* **Readiness.** The checker waits for the standard health service (`google.golang.org/grpc/health`, registered on the\n  same server) to answer `SERVING` for the empty service name.\n* **Dependencies.** `go.mod` and `go.sum` already list what the build needs (grpc, protobuf, modernc sqlite, health).\n  There is no network and no `go mod tidy` in the gate: use only packages those modules provide.\n* **Legacy acceptance scenarios.** `visible_spec.py` holds the customer's legacy acceptance scenarios; `spec.py` imports them, so the gate runs them. You do not change them.\n* **Gate.** `./check.sh` (generate, build, then the Lattice check of `spec.py`, layers C and D). Exit 0 = done.\ntotal 144\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 22 vivekgade  staff   704 Oct 31 16:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 vivekgade  staff   128 Oct 31 16:30 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 12 vivekgade  staff   384 Oct 31 16:30 .git\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff    42 Oct 31 16:25 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  1766 Oct 31 16:25 CONTEXT.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff   813 Oct 31 16:25 REQUIREMENTS.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff   177 Oct 31 16:25 buf.gen.yaml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff    37 Oct 31 16:25 buf.yaml\n-rwxr-xr-x@  1 vivekgade  staff   960 Oct 31 16:25 check.sh\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 vivekgade  staff    96 Oct 31 16:30 gen\n-rwxr-xr-x@  1 vivekgade  staff   349 Oct 31 16:25 generate.sh\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  1173 Oct 31 16:25 go.mod\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  7299 Oct 31 16:25 go.sum\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  1105 Oct 31 16:25 harness.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  1085 Oct 31 16:25 main.go\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 vivekgade  staff    96 Oct 31 16:25 proto\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff    91 Oct 31 16:25 pyproject.toml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff   241 Oct 31 16:25 shelf.go\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  3429 Oct 31 16:25 spec.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  1871 Oct 31 16:25 spec.trace.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff   743 Oct 31 16:25 studio.toml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff   546 Oct 31 16:25 visible_spec.py\n#!/bin/sh\n# The gate: build the server, check it against spec.py (layers C and D). The stubs in gen/ come from\n# `[grpc] generate` in studio.toml, which the loop runs before this gate (round 5, L2); run ./generate.sh by hand outside it.\n# Exit 0 = clean. LATTICE_REBUILD set (Studio running this as a gate) also writes metrics/last-check.json.\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\nmkdir -p bin\ngo build -o bin/toy-server .\nset -- --spec spec:SPEC --app harness:make_app --db harness:build_db --runtime harness:RUNTIME --layers CD \"$@\"\nif [ -n \"${LATTICE_REBUILD:-}\" ] || [ \"${TOY_CHECK_JSON:-0}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p metrics\n  set +e\n  uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\" --json > metrics/last-check.json\n  rc=$?\n  set -e\n  uv run python -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('metrics/last-check.json')); print(json.dumps({k: d[k] for k in d if k not in ('cases','findings')}, indent=1)[:3000])\" || true\n  exit $rc\nfi\nexec uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\"\n#!/bin/sh\n# The declared stub generator (studio.toml [grpc] generate): proto/ -> gen/ (buf, protoc-gen-go v1.36.5,\n# protoc-gen-go-grpc v1.5.1 from $TOY_TOOLS_BIN). gen/ is never committed and never edited by hand.\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\nif [ -n \"${TOY_TOOLS_BIN:-}\" ]; then PATH=\"$TOY_TOOLS_BIN:$PATH\"; export PATH; fi\nrm -rf gen\nbuf generate\nmodule example.com/toybuild\n\ngo 1.23\n\nrequire (\n\tgoogle.golang.org/grpc v1.71.0\n\tgoogle.golang.org/protobuf v1.36.5\n\tmodernc.org/sqlite v1.23.1\n)\n\nrequire (\n\tgithub.com/dustin/go-humanize v1.0.1 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/google/uuid v1.6.0 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/kballard/go-shellquote v0.0.0-20180428030007-95032a82bc51 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/mattn/go-isatty v0.0.16 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/remyoudompheng/bigfft v0.0.0-20230129092748-24d4a6f8daec // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/mod v0.17.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/net v0.34.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/sync v0.10.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/sys v0.29.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/text v0.21.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/tools v0.21.1-0.20240508182429-e35e4ccd0d2d // indirect\n\tgoogle.golang.org/genproto/googleapis/rpc v0.0.0-20250115164207-1a7da9e5054f // indirect\n\tlukechampine.com/uint128 v1.2.0 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/cc/v3 v3.40.0 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/ccgo/v3 v3.16.13 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/libc v1.22.5 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/mathutil v1.5.0 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/memory v1.5.0 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/opt v0.1.3 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/strutil v1.1.3 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/token v1.0.1 // indirect\n)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88a9c531-4815-45d8-9ef5-19f1c601720c","uuid":"71d6aa18-714d-4082-a9f8-f9908a6acca3","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:30:13.956Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Context: the Shelf service\n\nA gRPC server (Go, `google.golang.org/grpc`) over a SQLite file. The contract is `proto/toy/v1/shelf.proto`; the\nbehaviour is `REQUIREMENTS.md` / `spec.py`. You build the server; you do not change the proto, the spec, the harness,\nthe generator or this file.\n\n* **Stubs.** `gen/toy/v1/*.pb.go` is produced by `./generate.sh` (buf) from the proto and is rebuilt by every\n  `./check.sh`. Never write or edit anything under `gen/`. Import it as `toyv1 \"example.com/toybuild/gen/toy/v1\"`.\n* **Entry point.** A `package main` at the repository root (`go build -o bin/toy-server .`).\n* **Environment the checker sets.** `PORT`: listen for gRPC on `127.0.0.1:$PORT` (plaintext). `DB_PATH`: the SQLite file;\n  the table `items(id integer primary key autoincrement, name text not null unique, qty integer not null)` already\n  exists (the harness created it): do not create or migrate tables. Use `database/sql` with the pure-Go driver\n  `modernc.org/sqlite` (driver name `\"sqlite\"`; open `file:<DB_PATH>?_pragma=busy_timeout(10000)` and\n  `SetMaxOpenConns(1)`).\n* **Readiness.** The checker waits for the standard health service (`google.golang.org/grpc/health`, registered on the\n  same server) to answer `SERVING` for the empty service name.\n* **Dependencies.** `go.mod` and `go.sum` already list what the build needs (grpc, protobuf, modernc sqlite, health).\n  There is no network and no `go mod tidy` in the gate: use only packages those modules provide.\n* **Legacy acceptance scenarios.** `visible_spec.py` holds the customer's legacy acceptance scenarios; `spec.py` imports them, so the gate runs them. You do not change them.\n* **Gate.** `./check.sh` (generate, build, then the Lattice check of `spec.py`, layers C and D). Exit 0 = done.\ntotal 144\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 22 vivekgade  staff   704 Oct 31 16:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 vivekgade  staff   128 Oct 31 16:30 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 12 vivekgade  staff   384 Oct 31 16:30 .git\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff    42 Oct 31 16:25 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  1766 Oct 31 16:25 CONTEXT.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff   813 Oct 31 16:25 REQUIREMENTS.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff   177 Oct 31 16:25 buf.gen.yaml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff    37 Oct 31 16:25 buf.yaml\n-rwxr-xr-x@  1 vivekgade  staff   960 Oct 31 16:25 check.sh\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 vivekgade  staff    96 Oct 31 16:30 gen\n-rwxr-xr-x@  1 vivekgade  staff   349 Oct 31 16:25 generate.sh\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  1173 Oct 31 16:25 go.mod\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  7299 Oct 31 16:25 go.sum\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  1105 Oct 31 16:25 harness.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  1085 Oct 31 16:25 main.go\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 vivekgade  staff    96 Oct 31 16:25 proto\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff    91 Oct 31 16:25 pyproject.toml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff   241 Oct 31 16:25 shelf.go\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  3429 Oct 31 16:25 spec.py\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff  1871 Oct 31 16:25 spec.trace.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff   743 Oct 31 16:25 studio.toml\n-rw-r--r--@  1 vivekgade  staff   546 Oct 31 16:25 visible_spec.py\n#!/bin/sh\n# The gate: build the server, check it against spec.py (layers C and D). The stubs in gen/ come from\n# `[grpc] generate` in studio.toml, which the loop runs before this gate (round 5, L2); run ./generate.sh by hand outside it.\n# Exit 0 = clean. LATTICE_REBUILD set (Studio running this as a gate) also writes metrics/last-check.json.\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\nmkdir -p bin\ngo build -o bin/toy-server .\nset -- --spec spec:SPEC --app harness:make_app --db harness:build_db --runtime harness:RUNTIME --layers CD \"$@\"\nif [ -n \"${LATTICE_REBUILD:-}\" ] || [ \"${TOY_CHECK_JSON:-0}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p metrics\n  set +e\n  uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\" --json > metrics/last-check.json\n  rc=$?\n  set -e\n  uv run python -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('metrics/last-check.json')); print(json.dumps({k: d[k] for k in d if k not in ('cases','findings')}, indent=1)[:3000])\" || true\n  exit $rc\nfi\nexec uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\"\n#!/bin/sh\n# The declared stub generator (studio.toml [grpc] generate): proto/ -> gen/ (buf, protoc-gen-go v1.36.5,\n# protoc-gen-go-grpc v1.5.1 from $TOY_TOOLS_BIN). gen/ is never committed and never edited by hand.\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\nif [ -n \"${TOY_TOOLS_BIN:-}\" ]; then PATH=\"$TOY_TOOLS_BIN:$PATH\"; export PATH; fi\nrm -rf gen\nbuf generate\nmodule example.com/toybuild\n\ngo 1.23\n\nrequire (\n\tgoogle.golang.org/grpc v1.71.0\n\tgoogle.golang.org/protobuf v1.36.5\n\tmodernc.org/sqlite v1.23.1\n)\n\nrequire (\n\tgithub.com/dustin/go-humanize v1.0.1 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/google/uuid v1.6.0 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/kballard/go-shellquote v0.0.0-20180428030007-95032a82bc51 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/mattn/go-isatty v0.0.16 // indirect\n\tgithub.com/remyoudompheng/bigfft v0.0.0-20230129092748-24d4a6f8daec // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/mod v0.17.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/net v0.34.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/sync v0.10.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/sys v0.29.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/text v0.21.0 // indirect\n\tgolang.org/x/tools v0.21.1-0.20240508182429-e35e4ccd0d2d // indirect\n\tgoogle.golang.org/genproto/googleapis/rpc v0.0.0-20250115164207-1a7da9e5054f // indirect\n\tlukechampine.com/uint128 v1.2.0 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/cc/v3 v3.40.0 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/ccgo/v3 v3.16.13 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/libc v1.22.5 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/mathutil v1.5.0 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/memory v1.5.0 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/opt v0.1.3 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/strutil v1.1.3 // indirect\n\tmodernc.org/token v1.0.1 // indirect\n)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019iM5CogHL2XHLKBhCqU695","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
